**Research findings:**
- `main.py` already has `get_db_connection()`, `get_table_names()`, and `get_column_names()` — all reusable
- `PRAGMA table_info()` already used internally returns both column name (`row[1]`) and type (`row[2]`), so no new DB logic is needed
- Error handling pattern in `/chat` and `/health` is the model to follow for the new endpoint
- No new dependencies required

**Plan covers:**
- **`get_column_info()`** — new helper wrapping existing `PRAGMA table_info` logic, returns `[{"name": ..., "type": ...}]`
- **3 new Pydantic models** — `ColumnInfo`, `TableInfo`, `SchemaResponse` added after existing models
- **`GET /schema` route** — uses existing `get_db_connection()`, returns `SchemaResponse`, handles empty DB (200) and unreachable DB (500)
- **Root endpoint update** — adds `/schema` to the endpoints dict
- **`test_main.py`** — new test file with 4 test cases using in-memory SQLite fixtures
- **`API_DOCUMENTATION.md`** — new "Schema Endpoint" section with curl example and response shape

**Spec path:** `specs/add-schema-endpoint.md`
